dialogue.text:
{size=+6}THE GRIEF{/size}

{size=+2}Amelia carries the loss. Not as a weight to drag but as a seed to plant.
She will learn to live with grief. It will take longer than a year.
But she will learn.{/size}

{size=+6}THE ALCHEMIST{/size}

{size=+2}The Work is done — the first Work. The gold is real.
Amelia sees the world differently now. She always will.
Some would call it wisdom. Elena calls it sight.
The fire doesn't end. It just changes what it burns.{/size}

{size=+6}THE SCHOLAR{/size}

{size=+2}Amelia finds her vocation. Not just knowledge — understanding.
The mind that was hungry is still hungry, but now it knows
what it's hungry for. The library is her laboratory.
The gold is in the thinking.{/size}

{size=+6}THE COMPANION{/size}

{size=+2}Amelia discovers that the great work was never solitary.
The laboratory was the kitchen. The fire was love.
The gold is in the people who stayed.{/size}

{size=+6}THE HEALER{/size}

{size=+2}Amelia stays on the line. She will always stay on the line.
The wound becomes the gift. The one who was afraid
learns that courage isn't the absence of fear.
It's the phone ringing at 11pm, and picking up anyway.{/size}

{size=+6}THE WHOLE{/size}

{size=+2}Nothing is perfect. Everything is enough.
Amelia is not one thing — scholar, healer, seeker, friend.
She is all of them, imperfectly. The gold is in the balance.
The stone was always there. She can see it now.{/size}

{size=+6}THE BITTERSWEET{/size}

{size=+2}The most honest ending. Some gold, some lead.
Amelia doesn't know what comes next.
But the sea is still there, even when you can't see it.
The work is never finished. And that's okay.{/size}

{size=+6}THE CK: AMELIA{/size}

{size=+2}A story about a girl who went to university
and came back different.{/size}

{i}Things I know:{/i}
{i}1. I am not who I was.{/i}
{i}2. That's not the same as being who I want to be. But it's closer.{/i}
{i}3. Raj's daal cures most things. Not all things. But most.{/i}
